WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:17.614
Morb groaned as he returned to consciousness.

2
00:00:17.615 --> 00:00:21.673
For a moment he didn't remember where he was or what had happened.

3
00:00:21.674 --> 00:00:28.502
Then he saw the ruined house around him and the heavy beam lying beside him. His memory came rushing back.

4
00:00:28.503 --> 00:00:38.619
"Aargh!" he yelled, gnashing his teeth. "Those rotten children will pay for making a fool of me yet again!"

5
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.811
He rubbed his hands together and healed his aching head.

6
00:00:41.812 --> 00:00:45.053
Then he zapped himself back to the fortress.

7
00:00:45.054 --> 00:00:51.308
Several trolls were in the tower room staring dully at the map above the Secret Eye, as Morb had ordered.

8
00:00:51.309 --> 00:00:56.866
Morb glanced at the map, which was still blank. "Ridiculous," he snapped.

9
00:00:56.867 --> 00:01:01.522
Stalking over, he yanked the blink images out of the eye sockets.

10
00:01:01.523 --> 00:01:05.235
Immediately the map filled with glowing red dots.

11
00:01:05.236 --> 00:01:08.745
Morb glared at the trolls, who looked vaguely surprised.

12
00:01:08.746 --> 00:01:15.423
"Don't just stand there looking stupid!" he told them. "Go bring me some more Reds."

13
00:01:15.424 --> 00:01:22.236
The trolls exchanged a glance. One grunted, an image of sloppy gruel appearing over its head.

14
00:01:22.237 --> 00:01:26.381
"You'll get more food when you've earned it," Morb snapped.

15
00:01:26.382 --> 00:01:32.069
"Go!" He waited until the trolls zapped away, and then stomped downstairs.

16
00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:35.372
Boz was lying in his cell, weak and pale.

17
00:01:35.373 --> 00:01:41.465
Two trolls were coming out of the cell, carrying a large cauldron full of the bright blue leeches.

18
00:01:41.466 --> 00:01:45.876
"I hope you enjoyed today's treatment," Morb said sarcastically.

19
00:01:45.877 --> 00:01:51.965
"Normally I give my guests a day off to regain their magical energy between treatments.

20
00:01:51.966 --> 00:01:58.313
But since you are a former Magic Master, I thought you could handle two days in a row."

21
00:01:58.314 --> 00:02:02.338
Boz barely had the energy to lift his head and glare at Morb.

22
00:02:02.339 --> 00:02:05.703
"You won't get away with this," he croaked.

23
00:02:05.704 --> 00:02:10.566
"Don't try to talk too much, my friend," Morb warned with a sneer.

24
00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:15.838
"You need to rest before your next treatment. My leeches are always hungry.

25
00:02:15.839 --> 00:02:22.625
If you don't provide enough magic, they just might suck the life out of you one of these times."

26
00:02:22.626 --> 00:02:26.585
"Is that supposed to be a threat?" Boz said.

27
00:02:26.586 --> 00:02:30.681
"Because you don't scare me, Morb. You never did."

28
00:02:30.682 --> 00:02:37.740
"We'll see if you're still so confident when your grandson is in the cell next to you," Morb snarled.

29
00:02:37.741 --> 00:02:42.679
"Zann?" Panic suddenly filled Boz's face. "Is he here?"

30
00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:50.546
Morb didn't answer. Instead he turned and walked out of the cell, ordering the trolls to bring the cauldron of leeches.

31
00:02:50.547 --> 00:02:57.418
Boz continued to yell, but Morb ignored him and went into a small room at the end of the corridor.

32
00:02:57.419 --> 00:03:01.848
Inside was a stone pit full of firewood and kindling.

33
00:03:01.849 --> 00:03:05.427
Morb pointed, and instantly flames leaped out.

34
00:03:05.428 --> 00:03:09.328
With a grunt the trolls lifted the cauldron onto the fire.

35
00:03:09.329 --> 00:03:15.210
As the leeches cooked, the magic energy they had just ingested left their bodies.

36
00:03:15.211 --> 00:03:20.310
It rose up like steam, emerging from the cauldron in thick blue spirals.

37
00:03:20.311 --> 00:03:24.467
Morb leaned over the cauldron, breathing in the escaping magic.

38
00:03:24.468 --> 00:03:29.334
The steam burned his nose and throat, but he ignored the unpleasant feeling.

39
00:03:29.335 --> 00:03:34.922
For now he would continue to do things the slow, difficult way. But not for much longer.

40
00:03:34.923 --> 00:03:39.799
He was almost strong enough to put the next step of his plan into action.

41
00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:48.482
"Yes," he whispered, inhaling deeply, as more and more magical energy filled him.

42
00:03:48.483 --> 00:03:51.863
He felt powerful—more powerful than ever before.

43
00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:56.344
Boz had strong magic indeed. And now it was all his!

44
00:03:56.345 --> 00:03:59.290
Morb breathed in the last of the blue steam.

45
00:03:59.291 --> 00:04:09.260
Then he threw back his head and laughed, never noticing the big-eyed insect fluttering outside the tiny barred window at the top of the stone wall.

46
00:04:09.261 --> 00:04:14.104
"So your grandfather was suspicious of Morb from the start?" Gliss asked.

47
00:04:14.105 --> 00:04:19.435
Zann looked around at his friends. All of them, plus Zing, were still in the Hollow.

48
00:04:19.436 --> 00:04:25.876
They hadn't heard from Jev yet. So Zann was still reading as much as he could from his grandfather's diary.

49
00:04:25.877 --> 00:04:31.935
"Boz was suspicious of Morb," he said. "At least that's what he wrote in here.

50
00:04:31.936 --> 00:04:39.680
Boz stopped by the university a few days after Morb started working as an assistant animal caretaker at my parents' lab.

51
00:04:39.681 --> 00:04:44.007
At first Boz just thought Morb seemed secretive and shifty."

52
00:04:44.008 --> 00:04:46.394
"And then what?" Perda asked.

53
00:04:46.395 --> 00:04:54.039
"One day Boz caught Morb performing some nasty secret research on the lab animals," he said.

54
00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:57.428
Perda gasped. "What was he doing?"

55
00:04:57.429 --> 00:05:04.005
"Boz guessed that Morb was trying to figure out ways to steal magic from the creatures under his care."

56
00:05:04.006 --> 00:05:09.911
Darb looked stricken. "That's terrible!" he said, reaching out to stroke Zing's scales.

57
00:05:09.912 --> 00:05:14.676
"That sort of experimentation is strictly regulated by the Red Council.

58
00:05:14.677 --> 00:05:18.551
And caretakers are never supposed to take part in it."

59
00:05:18.552 --> 00:05:23.098
"I know," Zann said. "But I guess Morb didn't care.

60
00:05:23.099 --> 00:05:27.983
The second time Boz caught him, he was eating some leeches."

61
00:05:27.984 --> 00:05:31.992
"Eating them?" Gliss shuddered. "Yuck!"

62
00:05:31.993 --> 00:05:36.001
Zann nodded. "I guess it worked, at least a little.

63
00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:41.802
Morb was able to do enough magic to zap himself away before Boz could stop him."

64
00:05:41.803 --> 00:05:44.363
"What did Boz do?" Darb asked.

65
00:05:44.364 --> 00:05:50.386
"He told my parents that they should fire Morb and report him to the Council."

66
00:05:50.387 --> 00:05:51.579
"Did they?"

67
00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:56.244
"The next few pages aren't in very good shape." Zann bit his lip.

68
00:05:56.245 --> 00:05:58.904
"So I'm not sure what happened after that.

69
00:05:58.905 --> 00:06:04.599
The next part that's readable talks about Boz and me moving to Swamp Bottom."

70
00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:12.836
"Wow." Perda looked thoughtful. "Don't you find it odd that all that stuff happened right before your parents disappeared?"

71
00:06:12.837 --> 00:06:18.739
Zann shot her a look. "Are you saying that Morb had something to do with my parents' disappearance too?"

72
00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:22.643
Just then they heard Jev calling them from outside the Hollow.

73
00:06:22.644 --> 00:06:35.065
Perda jumped to her feet. "The spy fly must be back," she cried. "Let's go find out what it saw!"
